course: dictionary
lesson: 5306
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names, and some names have become slang. Karen is a girl's or woman's first name, like Sarah or Emma. In stories and at school, Karen is usually just a name. The words around it show you which meaning is used.
explain: Slang is informal language that a group of people uses, often friends or people online. A capital K tells you Karen is a name, but slang can use the same word with a different meaning. Ask: does this sentence make sense with a person's name, or with a label?
explain: The slang meaning is rude. A karen is a mocking word for a woman who complains loudly and demands to "speak to the manager". Because it is a label for real people, do not use it to tease someone or to be unkind.
fact: Karen is a girl's or woman's first name.
fact: Slang is informal language used by a group of people, such as friends or people online.
fact: «Speak to the manager» is a phrase people use when they want to complain to someone in charge.
fact: In slang, «a Karen» is a mocking label for a rude, demanding adult who makes trouble for shop workers.
fact: «Being a Karen» is a joke phrase for making a big fuss over something small.
exercise: Mum says, «And you'll never guess what Karen's — actually, no.» Is Karen a name in this sentence? | Yes, it means a shop | *Yes, it is a person's name | No, it means a park | No, it is always a rude word
exercise: Sarah and Karen are two girls in Year 5. What is Karen here? | A type of shop | *A girl's first name | A phrase meaning speak to the manager | A rude word for a woman
exercise: A child says, «Don't be a Karen, you're making a big fuss over a sweet.» What does being a Karen mean here? | *Making a big fuss over something small | Being very quiet and shy | Winning a race | Giving someone a present
test: Which meaning of karen is the rude slang meaning? | A kind of bread | A girl's first name | *A mocking label for a woman who complains loudly and demands to speak to the manager | A type of dog
test: The phrase «speak to the manager» is linked to which meaning? | *The slang meaning of a demanding complainer | A school subject | The name Karen | A pet's name
exam: Why should you not call a real person a Karen? | Because it is the name of a flower | Because it only means very happy | *Because it is a rude, mocking label that can hurt a real person | Because it is just a sound
